  "solution": {
    "text": "Among the given pairs Mo and W have the same atomic radius of <math><mn>139</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and this is due to Lanthanoid contraction.<br />This happens due to the poor screening ability of 4f electrons. The radius of other pairs are:<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>162</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>124</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>139</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>139</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>140</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal